# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# prediction_arb — environment file TEMPLATE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to the env file for the mode you are running and fill it in:
#
#     cp .env.example .env.paper        # for --mode paper / collect / historical
#     cp .env.example .env.live         # for --mode live  (see the warning below)
#
# Rules the application enforces (prediction_arb/core/config.py):
#   * Only ONE env file is loaded per run — the one named by the mode config
#     (`env_file:` in config/<mode>.yaml). Nothing else is read.
#   * A non-live env file that contains ANY key with "LIVE" in its name makes
#     startup REFUSE. Keep live credentials in .env.live only.
#   * Credentials are never logged (core/logging.py redaction filter).
#   * .env* files are git-ignored. Never commit them, never paste them into
#     chat, never email them.
#
# Everything below is optional: Kalshi PUBLIC market data (REST) needs no
# credentials at all, so --mode collect and --mode paper work with an empty
# env file. You need keys for WebSocket streaming, the demo environment, and
# (eventually) live trading.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Kalshi: paper / collect / historical ---------------------------------
# Create these at kalshi.com → account settings → API. You get a Key ID and a
# downloadable RSA private key (shown once — save it somewhere safe).
# Keep the PEM on ONE line, with \n escapes, exactly as shown.
#KALSHI_API_KEY_ID=
#KALSHI_PRIVATE_KEY_PEM="-----BEGIN RSA PRIVATE KEY-----\n...\n-----END RSA PRIVATE KEY-----"

# --- Kalshi: LIVE ONLY — put these in .env.live, never anywhere else --------
# A key created for live trading must carry the LIVE marker in its env-var
# name; the app refuses to load it in any other mode.
#KALSHI_LIVE_API_KEY_ID=
#KALSHI_LIVE_PRIVATE_KEY_PEM="-----BEGIN RSA PRIVATE KEY-----\n...\n-----END RSA PRIVATE KEY-----"

# --- Interactive Brokers / ForecastEx -------------------------------------
# No secrets go here. The Client Portal Gateway authenticates interactively in
# a browser (username + 2FA), and the gateway base URL lives in
# config/venues.yaml (`forecast_ex.cp_gateway_base`). To check or repair a
# gateway session use:
#     python scripts/ibkr_gateway_session.py --allow-self-signed
# See the 'Human action checklist' (H3) in docs/ROADMAP.md for the full beginner walkthrough.

# --- Optional: project root override --------------------------------------
# Only needed if you installed the package somewhere that cannot see the
# repository (see prediction_arb/core/paths.py for the resolution order).
#PREDICTION_ARB_HOME=/absolute/path/to/repo
